{
  "format": "protocol-app/facet-overrides-v1",
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Per-item effect calls that the derivation in scripts/facet-tags.mjs cannot make from `role` and `category` (TAXONOMY §2.3). Data rather than code because these are judgments, and a judgment nobody can read is a judgment nobody can correct. Every override names either a `rule` defined below or its own `why`.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "static-hold",
      "why": "The `mobility` shelf holds two different things and effect is the field that must tell them apart. A position taken to an end range and held lengthens tissue; it does not move a joint through its range. Twenty-three items, and the ledger would have counted every one of them as mobility work."
    },
    {
      "id": "through-range",
      "why": "The other half of the same shelf: CARs, cat-cow, hip switches, windmills — a joint driven through its own range rather than a tissue held at the end of one."
    }
  ],
  "overrides": [
